    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **51 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans (country code, space, national digits grouped in threes, e.g. `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec).\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a small static helper that splits the E.164 value into country code + national number and regroups the national digits in threes. Country-code detection (`+61`, `+1`, else 2-digit fallback) mirrors `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that derives `telephoneDisplay` via a static-method expression, matching the existing pattern used for `ageBand`, `identityKey`, etc.\n\n### Notable gotcha caught\nMy first attempt put the formatter as a `default String telephoneDisplay(String)` method on the mapper interface. MapStruct treated that `String \u2192 String` method as an eligible property-conversion and silently applied it while mapping the entity's `telephone` field during owner creation \u2014 corrupting the stored value to `+61 412 345 678` (with spaces), which then failed the `Owner.telephone` E.164 `@Pattern` at persist time and 500'd creation (breaking `Cp02` and others). Moving the logic to a standalone static class \u2014 the same convention the other derived fields already use \u2014 avoids polluting MapStruct's method candidate set. The raw `telephone` is now persisted untouched and `telephoneDisplay` is derived only on the response.",
